   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Methodology\n",
    "\n",
    "The project's technique entails a methodical procedure for examining past stock data, creating forecast models, and assessing each one's performance in order to choose a portfolio. Time-series data, including stock prices and market movements, is obtained from Yahoo Finance through the use of the yfinance library. Preprocessing is a crucial phase in which features are standardized with StandardScaler to guarantee consistent scaling and missing values are handled with the K-Nearest Neighbors Imputer (KNNImputer). To increase the trustworthiness of the data, outliers are also controlled. Regression forward selection is used to find the most influential characteristics, improving the model's focus and lowering the possibility of overfitting.\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset is divided into training and testing subsets for model development and evaluation, and portfolio performance is predicted using linear regression. Model correctness is evaluated using metrics such as Mean Squared Error (MSE) and Mean Absolute Error (MAE), and cross-validation guarantees robustness across different data splits. Heatmaps and line plots are two examples of visualizations that offer interpretive insights about model performance and data trends. Lastly, the results guide portfolio recommendations that emphasize the best possible asset allocation, and all procedures are well documented to guarantee reproducibility and openness.\n"
   ]
  },
