   "id": "a463489a-fc5b-4518-a127-d07bb36f946f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Importing the necessary libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "A number of libraries for data analysis, machine learning, and visualization are imported by the code. While pandas aids in data processing with DataFrames, yfinance is used to retrieve historical stock data from Yahoo Finance. For numerical computations, numpy is necessary since it makes handling arrays effective. Various plots, including time series and heatmaps, are created for visualization using matplotlib.pyplot and seaborn. OS facilitates the management of files and directories. KNNImputer is used in machine learning to manage missing data by using the nearest neighbors to impute values. StandardScaler scales models to a defined range, standardizing features to guarantee good performance. Cross_val_score evaluates model generalization using k-fold cross-validation, while train_test_split divides data into training and test sets for model assessment. Additionally, the algorithm use LinearRegression to predict continuous target variables. Mean_squared_error (MSE) and mean_absolute_error (MAE), which compare predicted and actual values to assess model accuracy, are used to measure performance. When combined, these libraries allow for reliable analysis, evaluation, and model construction. Additionally, the algorithm use Linear Regression to predict continuous target variables. Mean_squared_error (MSE) and mean_absolute_error (MAE), which compare predicted and actual values to assess model accuracy, are used to measure performance. When combined, these libraries allow for reliable analysis, evaluation, and model construction."
   ]
