    "## Importing and storing historical data (Data capture, processing and analysis and Error handling)\n",
    "\n",
    "This Python script downloads the daily closing values of a few chosen stocks for a given time period (December 1, 2022, to December 1, 2024) using the yfinance package (Reference 3). The script retrieves historical stock data for each ticker in the tickers list, which includes stock symbols. When data is available, dates are used as the index and closing prices are added as columns to a Pandas DataFrame. The DataFrame is saved in the current working directory as a CSV file called all_stock_data.csv once all tickers have been processed. To make sure the process is reliable, the script also manages exceptions during data fetching (such as ticker failures or empty data) and faults during file saving. The data for all of the tickers downloaded successfully, according to the results, and the CSV file, which is saved at the designated file directory, includes the closing prices for every ticker that was successful and describe the data after downloading to analyze.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Error Handling\n",
    "\n",
    "This code robustly handles errors during stock data processing. A try-except block surrounding the yf.download function handles API-related problems  like network outages or invalid tickers, so the application can log errors and keep processing other tickers without crashing. It ensures that existing files are preserved by renaming the output file to prevent overwriting and verifying that it already exists before saving the data. Furthermore, a try-except block encapsulates file-saving activities to gracefully manage permission difficulties or OS-related problems, delivering unambiguous error messages while preserving application stability.\n"
   ]
