    "## Identifying and handling missing values\n",
    "\n",
    "This code is used to identify and quantify missing values in the closing_prices DataFrame. First, it creates a DataFrame where each element is True if the corresponding value in closing_prices is missing (NaN) and False otherwise. Then it will calculates the total number of missing values for each column by summing up the True values in that column, providing a column-wise count of missing data. This information is displayed to help identify which stocks (columns) have gaps in their data. Finally, the code calculates and prints the total number of missing values across the entire DataFrame to give an overall view of the missing data in the dataset and a Barchart to display it graphically. This process ensures transparency before handling missing values using imputation or other methods."
   ]
