    "## Calculating the mean returns\n",
    "\n",
    "After applying exponential smoothing, the code snippet determines the mean returns of each stock in the data_smoothed Data Frame. It accomplishes this by first using the pct_change() function, which calculates the daily returns, to determine the percentage change of the stock prices. The average return for each stock for the whole period is then calculated using the mean() method. The mean_returns variable contains the results. The sort_values() method is then used to sort the mean_returns in descending order, making sure that the stocks with the highest average returns are at the top by passing in the ascending=False option. The stocks with the best average performance are then displayed by printing the sorted data.\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Mean Return} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\left( \\frac{P_i - P_{i-1}}{P_{i-1}} \\right)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P_i \\text{ is the price of the stock on day } i.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P_{i-1} \\text{ is the price of the stock on the previous day.}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "$$\n",
    "n \\text{ is the total number of days in the period.}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "This formula calculates the average percentage change (mean return) for each stock over the specified period by summing the daily returns and dividing by the total number of days.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
