   "source": [
    "## Correlation Matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "The below designed to select the top 10 stocks based on their mean returns, while ensuring that the selected stocks are not highly correlated with each other. It first calculates the correlation matrix for the stock data and then iterates through the sorted list of stocks (from highest to lowest mean return). The first stock is added to the selection list, and for each subsequent stock, it checks if its correlation with any already selected stock is below 0.7. If all correlations are under the threshold, the stock is added to the list. The process stops once 10 stocks are selected. This approach aims to create a diversified portfolio by minimizing the risk of selecting stocks that move in a similar direction, thus ensuring better diversification and reducing redundancy in the stock selection (Reference 5).\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Correlation Calculation:**\n",
    "\n",
    "   The correlation of two stocks \\( X \\) and \\( Y \\) is calculated as:\n",
    "\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "   \\text{Correlation}(X, Y) = \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n} (X_i - \\bar{X})(Y_i - \\bar{Y})}{\\sqrt{\\sum_{i=1}^{n} (X_i - \\bar{X})^2 \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (Y_i - \\bar{Y})^2}}\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\begin{aligned}\n",
    "&\\text{Where:} \\\\\n",
    "&X \\text{ and } Y \\text{ are the stock price series.} \\\\\n",
    "&X_i \\text{ and } Y_i \\text{ are the individual prices of stocks } X \\text{ and } Y. \\\\\n",
    "&\\bar{X} \\text{ and } \\bar{Y} \\text{ are the means of the prices of stocks } X \\text{ and } Y.\n",
    "\\end{aligned}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Stock Selection:**\n",
    "\n",
    "   For each new stock \\( X_{\\text{new}} \\), calculate its correlation with each of the previously selected stocks \\( X_{\\text{selected}} \\). If all correlations are less than 0.7, then add it to the list of selected stocks:\n",
    "\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "   \\text{If } |\\text{Correlation}(X_{\\text{new}}, X_{\\text{selected}})| < 0.7 \\text{ for all } X_{\\text{selected}}, \\text{ then add } X_{\\text{new}} \\text{ to the list.}\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Stopping Condition:**\n",
    "\n",
    "   The process will stop when the number of selected stocks \\( n = 10 \\):\n",
    "\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "   \\text{Stop when } \\text{len(selected stocks)} = 10\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "\n",
    "This ensures that the selected stocks have low correlation with each other, resulting in a diversified portfolio.\n"
   ]
  },
