   "source": [
    "### Annual return and annual risk (volatility)\n",
    "\n",
    "Determines the portfolio's yearly return and risk (volatility) based on the top ten chosen stocks. To calculate the portfolio's daily return, it first calculates the daily returns for each stock and then adds them together, giving each stock an equal weight. To determine the annual return, the mean daily return—which is calculated by averaging these daily returns—is then compounded over a period of 252 trading days the formula is mentioned above in the mean section. The portfolio variance is computed based on the relationships between the stocks in the portfolio, which are measured by the covariance matrix. The variance is used to calculate the portfolio's volatility (risk), which is then annualized by multiplying by 252 squared (Reference 12).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Portfolio Variance:\n",
    "The portfolio variance is calculated as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Portfolio Variance} = \\mathbf{w}^T \\cdot \\Sigma \\cdot \\mathbf{w}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- $\\mathbf{w}$ is the vector of portfolio weights.\n",
    "- $\\Sigma$ is the covariance matrix of the asset returns.\n",
    "- $\\mathbf{w}^T$ is the transpose of the portfolio weights vector.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Portfolio Volatility (Standard Deviation):\n",
    "The portfolio volatility (square root of the portfolio variance)(Reference 13):\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Portfolio Volatility} = \\sqrt{\\text{Portfolio Variance}}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Annual Volatility} = \\text{Portfolio Volatility} \\times \\sqrt{252}\n",
    "$$\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "0ef81db9-547f-414b-888b-5814e3c096bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Selected Top Stocks: ['RR.L', 'STAN.L', 'HL.L', 'SAGA.L', 'SMIN.L', 'SHEL.L', 'MNG.L', 'SSE.L', 'GSK.L', 'ITV.L']\n",
      "Annual Return: 15.27%\n",
      "Annual Volatility (Risk): 4.90%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Portfolio annual returns and risk for top 10 stocks\n",
    "daily_returns = data_smoothed[top_stocks].pct_change().dropna()\n",
    "weights = np.array([1/len(top_stocks)] * len(top_stocks))  # Equal weighting\n",
    "portfolio_daily_returns = daily_returns.dot(weights)\n",
    "mean_daily_return = portfolio_daily_returns.mean()\n",
    "cov_matrix = daily_returns.cov()\n",
    "annual_return = (1 + mean_daily_return) ** 252 - 1\n",
    "portfolio_variance = np.dot(weights.T, np.dot(cov_matrix, weights))\n",
    "portfolio_volatility = np.sqrt(portfolio_variance)\n",
    "annual_volatility = portfolio_volatility * np.sqrt(252)\n",
    "\n",
    "# results\n",
    "print(\"Selected Top Stocks:\", top_stocks)\n",
    "print(f\"Annual Return: {annual_return:.2%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Annual Volatility (Risk): {annual_volatility:.2%}\")"
   ]
  },
