    "#### Top stocks\n",
    "The stock data for the chosen top 10 stocks is extracted from the data_smoothed DataFrame, which holds the smoothed stock prices, using the line of code top_stocks_data = data_smoothed[top_stocks]. The list of stock tickers that have been determined to be the best options based on specific standards, including correlation, is called top_stocks. The code filters the data_smoothed DataFrame to keep only the columns that match to these chosen tickers by using data_smoothed[top_stocks]. The smoothed data for the selected top stocks is thus stored in the variable top_stocks_data, allowing for additional analysis or visualization for this selection of stocks.\n"
