    "## Evaluation metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "Three machine learning models—Linear Regression, Random Forest, and Gradient Boosting—have their evaluation metrics computed by this code. Mean Squared Error (MSE), R-squared (R²), Adjusted R-squared (R² adjusted), Mean Absolute Error (MAE), and cross-validation scores are among the important performance metrics that are calculated for every model. The model's error and fit on the test set (y_test and y_pred) are measured using the mean_squared_error, r2_score, and mean_absolute_error functions. The number of predictors in the model is taken into consideration while calculating adjusted R². In order to evaluate the generalizability of the model, cross_val_score also does 5-fold cross-validation to the training data. The number of test samples and features are denoted by the variables n and p, respectively. These measures aid in assessing the robustness and predictive performance of the models."
   ]
  },
