    "### Limitations of the work \n",
    "\n",
    "The reliance on the quality and availability of the dataset is one of the work's weaknesses because inconsistent, noisy, or incomplete data might have a detrimental impact on the generalization and performance of the model. Even with cross-validation, overfitting is still possible, particularly with sophisticated models like Random Forest and Gradient Boosting that could pick up on noise in the data rather than broad trends. Cross-validation aids in evaluating model performance, but if the distribution of the data changes, it might not accurately reflect real-world performance. Additionally, bias can be introduced by model and feature selection procedures, and other algorithms or hyperparameter configurations not discussed here may result in improved. Errors can occur while making predictions based on the complex external of the stocks based on the past returns making it hard to take into consideration the current real-time events for example if a war begins in another country or something like COVID-19 spreads around the world and the markets crash makes it very hard to predict the future prices based on these models also it fails to consider fundamentals of the company such as balance sheet credit history etc"
